-- title:
--   Pairwise disjoint base divisors off the cusp in L(2E-K)
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$ and write $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ N$ for the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the divisor expansions of level $N$; places of $F$ are the valuation subrings containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, distinct from $F$ itself and principal ideal rings, and $w.\mathrm{ord}$ is the associated normalised additive valuation. Assume the predicate `HasCanonicalDivisor` for $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq F$, i.e. that for each nonzero Kähler differential the function $v \mapsto v.\mathrm{ord}(v.\mathrm{differentialCoeff}\ \omega)$ is the coefficient function of a divisor, let $\omega \in \Omega[F/\overline{\mathbb Q}]$ be nonzero with chosen associated divisor $K = \mathrm{canonicalDivisorOf}\ h\omega$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Put $E = (2g+1)\,[\overline\infty]$, where $g$ is `genusFF` of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\overline\infty = \mathrm{cuspInftyBar}\ N$ is the $q$-adic place at infinity, and set $D = 2E - K$. The assertion is that there is a family $h : \mathrm{Fin}\ n \to F$ such that each $h_a$ is nonzero, each $h_a$ lies in the Riemann–Roch space of $D$ (i.e. $v(h_a) \le \exp(D v)$ for every place $v$), and for all $a \neq a'$ and every place $w \neq \overline\infty$ the two inequalities $\mathrm{ord}_w(h_a) + D(w) > 0$ and $\mathrm{ord}_w(h_{a'}) + D(w) > 0$ do not both hold.
--
--   In classical terms: the effective divisors $\operatorname{div}(h_a) + 2E - K$, of degree $2g+4$, can be chosen pairwise disjoint away from the cusp, which rests on the base-point freeness of the complete linear system $|2E-K|$ on $X_0(N)$ together with the fact that a vector space over an infinite field is not a finite union of proper subspaces. The family of $h_a$ serves as pole-clearing multipliers in the height-form estimates on $X_0(N)$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one).
